# SSR firmware upgrade

This menu item performs SSR (gateway / service router) firmware upgrades. The repository does not contain a function named `FirmwareManager.execute_ssr_firmware_upgrade`. The closest/authoritative implementation is the FirmwareOrchestrator in the mist-ops-platform worker: `mist-ops-platform/src/worker/deploy/firmware.py` (class FirmwareOrchestrator). That class performs validation and then invokes the Mist API via the MistEndpointService which resolves to the SDK endpoint `mistapi.api.v1.sites.devices.upgradeSiteDevices` (entity_type: `firmware_site`).

## Motivation

Provide a safe, auditable path to upgrade SSR (gateway) firmware programmatically while ensuring pre-upgrade validation and minimizing accidental destructive changes.

## Implementation summary (found in repository)

- Validation & payload building: `mist-ops-platform/src/worker/deploy/firmware.py` -> FirmwareOrchestrator
  - validate_upgrade(image_id, target_device_ids)
  - build_upgrade_payload(image_id, target_device_ids)
  - execute_upgrade(site_id, image_id, target_device_ids)

- Write to Mist used by orchestrator: `MistEndpointService.write_entity(...)` in `mist-ops-platform/src/shared/mist/endpoints.py`, which resolves to the SDK method: `mistapi.api.v1.sites.devices.upgradeSiteDevices`.

- Data export (CSV/SQLite) helpers are available as `DataExporter.write_with_format_selection(...)` in `MistHelper.py`, but the current firmware orchestrator `execute_upgrade()` does not call DataExporter.

## API calls / functions used

- FirmwareOrchestrator.execute_upgrade (mist-ops-platform/src/worker/deploy/firmware.py)
  - Calls MistEndpointService.write_entity(entity_type="firmware_site", ids={"site_id": site_id}, body=payload)
  - MistEndpointService resolves to SDK method: `mistapi.api.v1.sites.devices.upgradeSiteDevices(apisession, site_id, body=payload)`

- Related endpoints (registered in MistEntityRegistry):
  - firmware_device -> `mistapi.api.v1.sites.devices.upgradeDevice` (per-device)
  - firmware_org -> `mistapi.api.v1.orgs.devices.upgradeOrgDevices` (org-level)

## Inputs

- site_id: string (UUID of site)
- image_id: UUID (GoldenImage.image_id persisted in governance model)
- target_device_ids: list[UUID] (device ids to upgrade)
- Preconditions: GoldenImage must be in APPROVED state; device models must be compatible

## Outputs

- Returns ApiResult object (dataclass) from `MistEndpointService.write_entity`, with fields:
  - status_code: int
  - data: dict or list
  - ApiResult.success property indicates 2xx
- Side-effects: initiates upgrade on Mist cloud; logs via logger

## Acceptance criteria

- Pre-validation must run and reject upgrades when image is not APPROVED or any device is incompatible.
- The API call must be made via MistEndpointService and must call the SDK endpoint `upgradeSiteDevices` for site-scoped SSR upgrades.
- Successful path returns ApiResult.success == True (HTTP 2xx) and logs initiation with device count.
- Failures return ApiResult.success == False; errors are logged and surfaced to caller.
- No silent destructive actions: user must explicitly confirm before upgrades when triggered interactively.

## Error handling

- Validation errors: `validate_upgrade()` returns `{"valid": False, "errors": [...]}`; `execute_upgrade()` raises RuntimeError if validation fails.
- API call failure: `ApiResult.success == False` -> logged as error with result.error; return ApiResult to caller (caller decides subsequent flow).
- Network/timeout: MistEndpointService wraps SDK response; callers should treat non-2xx / status_code None as failure; caller code should catch and log exceptions.

## Rollback strategy (destructive operations)

- Firmware upgrade is destructive; automatic rollback is not provided. Recommended strategy:
  - Preventive: require pre-validation (image approved + model compatibility) and (for UI/interactive) a human confirmation step.
  - Operational: implement scheduled/approved rollout job model (mist-ops-platform already has Deploy/ScheduledJob abstractions) and staged rollouts with checkpoints and canary waves.
  - Recovery: if a bad firmware is deployed, operators must use Mist portal/SDK to re-image or re-upgrade to a known-good version. Provide a documented remediation playbook instead of an automated rollback.

## Notes

- The explicit function name `FirmwareManager.execute_ssr_firmware_upgrade` was not found in the repo. Use FirmwareOrchestrator.execute_upgrade as the canonical implementation and MistEndpointService to perform the SDK call.
- DataExporter is available (DataExporter.write_with_format_selection in MistHelper.py) but not used by firmware orchestrator — see remediation in tasks.
